  "problem": "Expressed in its simplest form, $\\sqrt{{16}^{2}}=${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that if $a\\ge 0,$ then\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{a}^{2}}=a.\n$$\n\nIn our case, since the number under the square root ($\\sqrt{}$) is already written as a square, we obtain the answer immediately:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{16}^{2}}=16\n$$",
